.TH OOBE-TUI 1 2026-10-19 "Peios installer 0.1.13"
.SH NAME
oobe-tui \- terminal surface for Peios first-boot setup
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B oobe-tui
.RB [ \-\-socket
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-kind
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-plain ]
.RB [ \-\-size
.IR COLSxROWS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B oobe-tui
renders the first-boot conversation owned by
.BR oobed (8).
Leaving setup unfinished does not retire it; the flow is offered again on the
next boot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " PATH"
Connect to PATH instead of
.IR /run/oobed.sock .
.TP
.BI \-\-kind " NAME"
Request an MSIP kind other than
.BR oobe .
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Use the conservative serial-console presentation.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " COLSxROWS"
Override terminal geometry. Both dimensions must be non-zero.
.TP
.BR \-h , " \-\-help"
Show command help.
.TP
.BR \-V , " \-\-version"
Show the program version.
.SH SECURITY
The frontend needs access to the daemon's socket.
It presents the conversation and does not perform the daemon's disk or
account operations.
The supplied first-boot service runs
.B oobe-tui
as SYSTEM because no administrator account exists yet.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The interface returned normally, including a user-requested exit.
This status alone does not establish successful installation or setup.
.TP
.B 1
The frontend could not connect to the daemon.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command-line arguments.
.TP
.B 101
An unrecoverable terminal or protocol operation caused a Rust panic.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLUMNS
Fallback column count when the terminal cannot report its size.
.TP
.B LINES
Fallback row count when the terminal cannot report its size.
The
.B \-\-size
option overrides size discovery.
Without a usable size, the frontend falls back to 80 columns and 24 rows.
.SH NOTES
The renderer determines the terminal size at startup.
Press Ctrl+L to repaint after unrelated console output disrupts the form.
Closing the frontend does not cancel a running daemon job.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR oobed (8)
